  "title": " The Hidden Deal Killer You\u2019re Probably Ignoring",
  "date": "2025-05-02T14:31:10.276Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n The Hidden Deal Killer You\u2019re Probably Ignoring\nHi Sara,\nWant to know one of the top reasons business sales die at the last minute?\nThe landlord.\nNo one thinks about them until they\u2019re the only thing standing between you and closing\u2014and by then, you have zero leverage.\nThis week, I saw a deal collapse days before closing because of a lease issue. The buyers were relocating, everything was lined up\u2026 and then they realized they had to personally guarantee the lease. Just like that, the deal was dead.\nWhy Landlords Hold All the Cards\nIf your business is in a prime location, the landlord knows they can fill that space instantly. So why should they rush to approve a new tenant?\nThey don\u2019t need to play ball, and if you wait too long to negotiate, they\u2019ll have all the power.\nHow to Avoid This Mess\n\nGet the landlord involved early. Yes, confidentiality matters, but waiting until the end gives them every reason to say no.\n\nKnow that personal guarantees are standard. If you\u2019re hoping to avoid one, be prepared to prepay rent or put up extra security.\n\nIf you\u2019re a seller, don\u2019t assume the lease transfer will be easy. Buyers might be excited to take over your business, but if the landlord refuses to assign the lease, the deal is dead.\n\nLessons from the Trenches\nI\u2019ve seen deals where landlords have:\nRefused to assign a lease because they liked the current tenant and didn\u2019t want to risk a change.\n\nRejected SBA-required lease terms, which make the bank the first priority if the business defaults. Landlords hate this.\n\nChanged their mind at the last second, leaving the buyer stranded.\n\nIf you\u2019re in a transaction right now, consider this your warning shot\u2014figure out the lease situation before you\u2019re deep into due diligence.\nIf you want more insights on how to keep your deal from falling apart at the finish line, check out our course offerings on Deal Academy.\nTo deals that actually close,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nBusiness Consultant & Founder of Deal Academy\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
